{#- What the agent's lander lands, and for whom: claude-land@.service.j2 and 50-claude-land.rules.j2
import these as `pins`. A template's own assignment outranks every inventory value, so an agent
PR that edits only host_vars cannot repoint the unit, widen the branches or authors it lands,
let another Unix user start it, or name another approver. The inventory is off the approval
list (docs/claude-agent-user.md, "The approval floor"), and this file is on it. Each value is a
literal, except the checkout, which follows the operator's account as the unit's User= does.
ansible/tests/setup/test_claude_lander.py holds them equal to the agent profile they describe.
-#}
{%- set unit = "homelab-claude-land" -%}
{%- set checkout = "/home/" ~ sys_user ~ "/server" -%}
{%- set branch_prefix = "worktree-claude+" -%}
{%- set author = "DanielClaudeBot" -%}
{%- set agent_user = "claude" -%}
{%- set approver = "DanielH2018" -%}
